I don't have a file-editing tool available in this session (only read/search/memory tools), so I can't apply these changes directly — here are the exact edits to make, based on the research above.

## Root cause

Two iframe layers never receive `dir`, because a `srcdoc` document (and any cross-document boundary) never inherits `dir` from its embedder even when same-origin:
1. **`.css-example` live-preview iframes** (`buildExampleSrcdoc` in [tools/demo/src/srcdoc.ts](tools/demo/src/srcdoc.ts)) — opaque origin (`sandbox="allow-scripts"` only, no `allow-same-origin`), so it can't read the parent at all. `dir` must be baked in at build time.
2. **The `/play` runner's own result iframe** (`ctx.resultFrame.srcdoc` in [tools/demo/runner/main.ts](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L321)) — same-origin with its parent (already reads `window.parent.document.documentElement.classList` for dark mode, `isDark()` at line 45), so it *can* read `dir` directly, but doesn't yet.

## Patch 1 — `tools/demo/src/srcdoc.ts`

```ts
/** Options for {@link buildExampleSrcdoc}. */
export interface ExampleSrcdocOptions {
  /** Stylesheet URLs to load into the iframe's `<head>` (tokens, components, utilities, icons, …). */
  cssUrls: readonly string[];
  /** Wrap `html` in the shared `.instui-card` surface (default `true`). */
  card?: boolean;
  /** Text direction for the isolated document's `<html>` — doesn't inherit across the srcdoc boundary. */
  dir?: "ltr" | "rtl";
}
```

```ts
export function buildExampleSrcdoc(html: string, options: ExampleSrcdocOptions): string {
  const links = options.cssUrls.map((href) => `<link rel="stylesheet" href="${href}">`).join("");
  const body = options.card === false ? html : `<div class="instui-card">${html}</div>`;
  return (
    `<!doctype html><html dir="${options.dir ?? "ltr"}"><head><meta charset="utf-8">${links}` +
    `<style>body{padding:var(--instui-spacing-space-md, 1rem);margin:0}</style></head>` +
    `<body class="pantoken-prose">${body}${BOOT_SCRIPT}</body></html>`
  );
}
```

## Patch 2 — `tools/demo/src/index.ts`

```ts
export interface LiveExampleOptions {
  match: (relativePath: string) => boolean;
  /** Build the preview block. `relativePath` is the page's markdown-it `env.relativePath`, for locale/direction lookups. */
  wrap: (html: string, flags: Set<string>, relativePath: string) => string;
}
```

At the call site (~line 524):
```ts
      if (live.match(relativePath) && !isOverlay(html)) {
        return `${rendered}\n${live.wrap(html, flags, relativePath)}\n`;
      }
```

## Patch 3 — `docs/.vitepress/config.ts` (~line 654)

```ts
          wrap: (html: string, flags: Set<string>, relativePath: string) => {
            const locale = NON_ROOT_LOCALES.find((key) => relativePath.startsWith(`${key}/`)) ?? "root";
            const doc = buildExampleSrcdoc(html, {
              cssUrls,
              card: !flags.has("-nocard"),
              dir: LOCALES[locale].dir,
            });
            return (
              `<div class="css-example-frame">` +
              `<iframe class="pantoken-demo__frame css-example" sandbox="allow-scripts" ` +
              `title="Live example" loading="lazy" srcdoc="${escapeSrcdoc(doc)}"></iframe>` +
              `${FULLSCREEN_BUTTON_HTML}</div>`
            );
          },
```
(`NON_ROOT_LOCALES` and `LOCALES` are already imported/used in this file.)

## Patch 4 — `tools/demo/runner/main.ts`

Add next to `isDark()` (~line 39):
```ts
/** Whether the embedding page reads right-to-left; doesn't cross the iframe boundary automatically. */
function isRtl(): boolean {
  try {
    if (window.parent && window.parent !== window) {
      return window.parent.document.documentElement.dir === "rtl";
    }
  } catch {
    // Cross-origin parent.
  }
  return false;
}
```

In `render()` (~line 298), mirror the runner's own chrome direction and bake it into the result srcdoc:
```ts
function render(ctx: RunnerCtx): void {
  const scheme = schemeName();
  document.documentElement.style.colorScheme = isDark() ? "dark" : "light";
  document.documentElement.dir = isRtl() ? "rtl" : "ltr";
  ...
  ctx.resultFrame.srcdoc =
    `<!doctype html><html dir="${isRtl() ? "rtl" : "ltr"}" data-pantoken-theme="${ctx.currentTheme}" style="color-scheme:${scheme}"><head>...`
```

Extend the live-sync observer's `attributeFilter` (~line 624) to also catch `dir` toggles:
```ts
      new MutationObserver(() => applyTheme(ctx)).observe(window.parent.document.documentElement, {
        attributes: true,
        attributeFilter: ["class", "dir"],
      });
```

## Tests to update
- `tools/demo/tests/srcdoc.test.ts` — add a case asserting `dir="rtl"` appears when `{ dir: "rtl" }` is passed, and `dir="ltr"` by default.
- `tools/demo/tests/index.test.ts` — the `wrap` fixtures there only destructure `(html, flags)`, which stays valid since `relativePath` is an added third parameter (structurally compatible); no changes required unless a test wants to assert the passed `relativePath`.

Since I can't run `vp check`/tests or write these files myself right now, let me know if you'd like me to switch to an edit-capable mode to actually apply them.

